{"title":"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the three sides of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a>, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, be the angles opposite them. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/89445e636a09e492ba5842199c0481c9440a2ee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=1989c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />, find\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858c49b569dc76c503dbdbfa8d0b78fd2c04fe1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cot \\gamma}{\\cot \\alpha+\\cot \\beta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"102\" height=\"40\" /></center>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Quick_and_Easy),_similar_idea_to_Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Quick and Easy), similar idea to Solution 8</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We draw the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitude</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, to get two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangles</a>.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca7f7ca9366088b0274daace75e09ea38876ae3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(170); pair A = (0,0), B = (3, 0), C = (1, 4); pair P = .5*(C + reflect(A,B)*C); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(C--P, dotted); draw(rightanglemark(C,P, B, 4)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$a$&quot;, (B+C)/2, NE); label(&quot;$b$&quot;, (A+C)/2, NW); label(&quot;$c$&quot;, (A+B)/2, S); label(&quot;$h$&quot;, (C+P)/2, E);[/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"285\" /></center>\n<p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec41559cf284f62623cf91098669e80e56e423e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{\\alpha}+\\cot{\\beta}=\\frac{c}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"136\" height=\"33\" />, from the definition of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cotangent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cotangent\">cotangent</a>.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d711d054d7598f90c6422e39c93d63b7573261aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\frac{2K}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"39\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b593cd08084e033f376bf56106200c86f265dad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{\\alpha}+\\cot{\\beta}=\\frac{c^2}{2K}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>By identical logic, we can find similar expressions for the sums of the other two cotangents:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d9f2824b336122f37af5a7b54520da33bcff1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cot \\alpha + \\cot \\beta &amp;= \\frac{c^2}{2K} \\\\ \\cot \\beta + \\cot \\gamma &amp;= \\frac{a^2}{2K} \\\\ \\cot \\gamma + \\cot \\alpha &amp;= \\frac{b^2}{2K}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"157\" height=\"130\" />\nAdding the last two equations, subtracting the first, and dividing by 2, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/017416a7ab14f8cf21471cdd0c23baa8d75d0ae6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cot \\gamma = \\frac{a^2 + b^2 - c^2}{4K}.\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"39\" />\nTherefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/99430a5b738f20772b4aa5f054855b4aa110bea9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\cot \\gamma}{\\cot \\alpha + \\cot \\beta} &amp;= \\frac{(a^2 + b^2 - c^2)/(4K)}{c^2/(2K)} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{a^2 + b^2 - c^2}{2c^2} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1989 c^2 - c^2}{2c^2} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1988}{2} = \\boxed{994}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"283\" height=\"178\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_cosines\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Law of cosines\">law of cosines</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02371d40aeb597945d74f2dbc29610c814b90e75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos \\gamma = \\frac{a^2 + b^2 - c^2}{2ab}.\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"39\" /> So, by the extended <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_sines\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Law of sines\">law of sines</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7cf5daa461bfde0b14812e810dcec6e214b853e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cot \\gamma = \\frac{\\cos \\gamma}{\\sin \\gamma} = \\frac{a^2 + b^2 - c^2}{2ab} \\cdot \\frac{2R}{c} = \\frac{R}{abc} (a^2 + b^2 - c^2).\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"43\" />\nIdentical logic works for the other two angles in the triangle.  So, the cotangent of any angle in the triangle is directly proportional to the sum of the squares of the two adjacent sides, minus the square of the opposite side.  Therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11dba4002d3435591de895b0c5271267b06b4629.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\cot \\gamma}{\\cot \\alpha + \\cot \\beta} = \\frac{a^2 + b^2 - c^2}{(-a^2 + b^2 + c^2) + (a^2 - b^2 + c^2)} = \\frac{a^2 + b^2 - c^2}{2c^2}.\\]\" width=\"502\" height=\"44\" />\nWe can then finish as in solution 1.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We start as in solution 1, though we'll write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> for the area.  Now we evaluate the numerator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c22641e38f6d8db17fa3456f720ddf933d3fad77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cot{\\gamma}=\\frac{\\cos{\\gamma}}{\\sin{\\gamma}}\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>From the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a> and the sine area formula, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a0f2e5fc5d65cd3432c6f33311cf8fb6106fc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\cos{\\gamma}&amp;=\\frac{1988c^2}{2ab}\\\\ \\sin{\\gamma}&amp;= \\frac{2A}{ab}\\\\ \\cot{\\gamma}&amp;= \\frac{\\cos \\gamma}{\\sin \\gamma} = \\frac{1988c^2}{4A} \\end{align*}\" width=\"181\" height=\"131\" />\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfaa40707a9889bd2cb18733448369b11769a5d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cot \\gamma}{\\cot \\alpha+\\cot \\beta}=\\frac{\\frac{1988c^2}{4A}}{\\frac{c^2}{2A}}=\\frac{1988}{2}=\\boxed{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"302\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23b6c7b9511498d167e2bee4ef0fa01f56026642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cot{\\alpha} + \\cot{\\beta} &amp;= \\frac {\\cos{\\alpha}}{\\sin{\\alpha}} + \\frac {\\cos{\\beta}}{\\sin{\\beta}} = \\frac {\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos{\\beta} + \\cos{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}}{\\sin{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac {\\sin{(\\alpha + \\beta)}}{\\sin{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}} = \\frac {\\sin{\\gamma}}{\\sin{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"437\" height=\"90\" />\n</p><p>By the Law of Cosines,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c4ea7553b97c6627c49aafa494ec474a6caab3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\cos{\\gamma} = c^2 = 1989c^2 - 2ab\\cos{\\gamma} \\implies ab\\cos{\\gamma} = 994c^2\\]\" width=\"497\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/f/f1f7520b0dec0c49dbbc65d32486eb260da3af1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac {\\cot{\\gamma}}{\\cot{\\alpha} + \\cot{\\beta}} &amp;= \\frac {\\cot{\\gamma}\\sin{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}}{\\sin{\\gamma}} = \\frac {\\cos{\\gamma}\\sin{\\alpha}\\sin{\\beta}}{\\sin^2{\\gamma}} = \\frac {ab}{c^2}\\cos{\\gamma} = \\frac {ab}{c^2} \\cdot \\frac {994c^2}{ab}\\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{994}\\end{align*}\" width=\"583\" height=\"73\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Use Law of cosines to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e91951a0696df280d399e8767ef5f79b7324c0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos(\\gamma)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"19\" /> or therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/51492e76cf335bc77b17cf15ce28265a32b2bdfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\gamma)=\\frac{994c^2}{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />.  Next, we are going to put all the sin's in term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2f8845b18ace360914e19e68c362c6f7121587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />.  We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a085686976ec0538431081f4c996b33c3f564a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\gamma)=\\frac{c\\sin(a)}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />.  Therefore, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7efbc3ae6a9ec6098381e394543d8b555ab0e9df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\gamma)=\\frac{994c}{b\\sin a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Next, use Law of Cosines to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2128ce8f2508bd59c29ab1c04c6cee0b09e288d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2=a^2+c^2-2ac\\cos(\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/90660065f09c6f368f634b165d210ba6147ab90f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\beta)=\\frac{a^2-994c^2}{ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"39\" />.  Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615fef5e4d72cdf6f1d3a3a81fb29709f7e891c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\beta)=\\frac{b\\sin(a)}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"38\" />.  Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce9ac6c3ef5eb9ae47ad5e3c98878a4cb820f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\beta)=\\frac{a^2-994c^2}{bc\\sin(a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" />.  \n</p><p>Lastly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073fa38166e25c61d4f84e798a8748c3e738c6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\alpha)=\\frac{b^2-994c^2}{bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"157\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad4033a84eb5179fca9df127cb5def28fca7d02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\alpha)=\\frac{b^2-994c^2}{bc\\sin(a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"157\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea3c3a35f6ed54880cad957fa51836e90719c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cot(\\gamma)}{\\cot(\\beta)+\\cot(\\alpha)}=\\frac{\\frac{994c}{b\\sin a}}{\\frac{a^2-994c^2+b^2-994c^2}{bc\\sin(a)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"277\" height=\"51\" />.  After using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/89445e636a09e492ba5842199c0481c9440a2ee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=1989c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7baf33708cd9c999a429ba617c4680e74ca501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{994c*bc\\sin a}{c^2b\\sin a}=\\boxed{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/7896b37be6a06f2319e253c6fa1a18c7b4870a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(180-\\alpha-\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e666aca5f1673e13b6c473149dc9a8e3411a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cot \\gamma}{\\cot \\alpha+\\cot \\beta} = \\frac{\\frac{-\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta}{\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)}}{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta} = \\frac{(\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta)^2-\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta}{\\tan^2 \\alpha + 2\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta +\\tan^2 \\beta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"500\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>WLOG, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are legs of right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59a3e038470528dd3b698f0d77ffa6a7b9bfa5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta = 90^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4cc644ec8a1c3623c13ed3d14904096a0d87b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>By the Pythagorean theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c97d27c4f1fbc104ccf8f6780155126573b8f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2=a^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, and the given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d40f403dc26a9669491083cdc7a80c21fcb92843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=1989$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />. Solving the equations gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3a0e1633bf82c309903d1371199e67944af3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\sqrt{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba6668e011abfea8e4997c9ad17f5fc6dbf021e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\sqrt{995}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f3684f24bb411a46ade3b87fb1247e798d231a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\beta = \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/63935291b74f99ac3f5ce8a04a85c3466344b07a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\alpha = \\sqrt{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Our derived equation equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e68e1e031c1174cca4d5ffe79669ad4e7665d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2 \\alpha$\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07633647dee0aabed465bd312cc25e47637dc3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> approaches infinity.\nEvaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e68e1e031c1174cca4d5ffe79669ad4e7665d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2 \\alpha$\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d041fda5dd337f4d529936adfef8274053ffef37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>As in Solution 1, drop an altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2c62552c49d61d60b3053ae078ef725e1bf79b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = x, BP = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd61091c8c8e5ee3e9ff7a2580f8c81786391de1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(170); pair A = (0,0), B = (3,0), C = (1,4); pair P = .5*(C + reflect(A,B)*C); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(C--P, dotted); draw(rightanglemark(C,P, B , 4)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, S); label(&quot;$x$&quot;, (A+P)/2, S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;, (B+P)/2, S); label(&quot;$a$&quot;, (B+C)/2, NE); label(&quot;$b$&quot;, (A+C)/2, NW); label(&quot;$c$&quot;, (A+B)/2, S); label(&quot;$h$&quot;, (C+P)/2, E);[/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"285\" /></center>\n<p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17baf8c0f4a73dbf3bc0ab2cad5d4d35867c3d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{\\alpha} = \\frac{1}{\\tan{\\alpha}} = \\frac{x}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"149\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e27bfc338c97a558b7b240f3b70e69a781453a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{\\beta} = \\frac{1}{\\tan{\\beta}} = \\frac{y}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"148\" height=\"42\" />. We can calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/468d468fdea28db0a104d50e727903ae25b711fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{\\gamma}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent_addition_formula\" title=\"Tangent addition formula\">tangent addition formula</a>, after noticing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e4125ab6f2969c893de7c8d69fb89fcc8e551fd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{\\gamma} = \\frac{1}{\\tan{\\gamma}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"107\" height=\"42\" />. So, we find that \n\\begin{align*}\n\\cot{\\gamma} &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\tan{\\gamma}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{1}{\\frac{\\frac{x}{h} + \\frac{y}{h}}{1 - \\frac{xy}{h^2}}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{1}{\\frac{(x+y)h}{h^2 - xy}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{h^2 - xy}{(x+y)h}.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>So now we can simplify our original expression:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\cot{\\gamma}}{\\cot{\\alpha} + \\cot{\\beta}} &amp;= \\frac{\\frac{h^2 - xy}{(x+y)h}}{\\frac{x + y}{h}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{h^2 - xy}{(x+y)^2}.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>But notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443f7fae6516d94077957537382416192d17ea3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, so this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/68310cee60de9a951620d0dd06259b3ed299c0b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{h^2 - xy}{c^2}.\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"39\" />\nNow note that we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> to calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319c4d6557b81962a2076f2017878709cf698551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aad958b7d4209e01fd96f068791dba6405872ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h^2 = \\frac{a^2 - y^2 + b^2 - x^2}{2}.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"39\" />\nSo our expression simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a8da60f2f844fb49ddf2aee3eb7bc558dd48de6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1989c^2 - (x+y)^2}{2c^2}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"39\" />\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a7d3f3c11edb8e151cc88dfd8f9b74c3eabf9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 = 1989c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> from the problem and that there is another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d87e591fc03966e4eecead4f8c009e03bdb53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{2xy}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" /> after the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319c4d6557b81962a2076f2017878709cf698551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> in our expression. Again note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443f7fae6516d94077957537382416192d17ea3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, so it again simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1bfc024d55241e6d625cb8c5adfe7fc0b23d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1988c^2}{2c^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"41\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d041fda5dd337f4d529936adfef8274053ffef37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Yiyj1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Yiyj1 (page does not exist)\">Yiyj1</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Quick_and_Easy)\">Solution 8 (Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since no additional information is given, we can assume that triangle ABC is right with the right angle at B.\nWe can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> to say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81997311a98a234ac8ca7b6f86080f42318f0099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c^2+a^2=b^2\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> \nWe can now solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11dc97227e52f4c322c1f7742bb8f6370060a9d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c^2+a^2=1989c^2-a^2\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/25665322631f87b5ce075b9e0f980a92e62fb6a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2=994c^2\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd8013ae30af85de8ede4cc4563ab5909004fa4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=\\sqrt{994}c\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Using the definition of cotangent\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd4ed820f8ff2b014f897f85c2c7a314981c76ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[cot(A)=\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{994}}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b72b83997955f1c1b17ac68c31072ba11d9cab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[cot(B)=cot(90)=0\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c1fa5601f56351fae2febb4191e2127cfb47be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[cot(C)=\\frac{a}{c}=\\sqrt{994}\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"32\" />\nPlugging into our desired expression, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d041fda5dd337f4d529936adfef8274053ffef37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Ms0001&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Ms0001 (page does not exist)\">ms0001</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Quick_and_Easy.29.2C_similar_idea_to_Solution_8\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Quick_and_Easy),_similar_idea_to_Solution_8\">Solution 9 (Quick and Easy), similar idea to Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Quick and Easy), similar idea to Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Assume the triangle is isosceles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4cc644ec8a1c3623c13ed3d14904096a0d87b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.  \nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9208828d228aeb8a08ebcbaaa4c21775f65f9ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2=1989$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2bb4e658c7037d2956f44ec0647145e26ce25d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rightarrow a=b=\\sqrt{\\frac{1989}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"149\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Since this is an isosceles triangle, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/186816cbb8c8214915c207e2a94320c629796c09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1a037b5684a80dbacdbe4ddd6b1b36606b951e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, by just drawing the height.  \nVia Pythagorean Theorem, the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/325ce94a421bbc5eb294865c1a598413dc6a5387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3977}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24a28904ab0b66e858864cdb7e305c1d62a8a338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\alpha) = \\tan(\\beta) = \\sqrt{3977}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"24\" />.  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06fbcff275d8896786e3f65c827db255b94c664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\gamma) = \\tan(180-(\\alpha+\\beta)) = -\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"353\" height=\"20\" />.  \nVia tangent sum formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f603875a9584bd74f9e2aab7083b53dcd7a62461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3977}}{1988}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba220c7b8b8f60999e05b99d678b9057f65a2b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\gamma) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3977}}{1988}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/6/ea64ba577e6151a1e5f0f95e5d7aaa20edca8ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{\\tan(\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"127\" height=\"43\" />,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0787ee1e7dcb2fe6e70bfd8660ebdc7b0b2120bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\alpha) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3977}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9abfcc867be6869dce8784fc29c3ba110a70010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\beta) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3977}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"131\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb1810765feb499a1033c29b87f4ac71caae1bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\gamma) = \\frac{1988}{\\sqrt{3977}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging this in, almost everything cancels and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b1060e15bfbe4c1fbaf3beb49adf8704328650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1988}{2} = \\boxed{994}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME\" title=\"1989 AIME\">1989 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div sty